{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":35.11000061035156,"text":"A black, heavy engine with a tall chimney built in 1813 to 1814 at Wylam Colliery in the north of England by William Headley and his engineers, it is the oldest surviving steam locomotive in the world. It hauled coal wagons down to the river at the speed of a person walking fast, and it puffed so loudly that the locals nicknamed it Puffing Billy. It worked until 1862, almost 50 years, and then came straight to the museum. The first locomotives that carried passengers, a few years later, learned from its mistakes.","words":[{"word":"A","start":0,"end":0.47999998927116394},{"word":"black","start":0.47999998927116394,"end":0.9599999785423279},{"word":"heavy","start":1.440000057220459,"end":1.440000057220459},{"word":"engine","start":1.440000057220459,"end":1.7799999713897705},{"word":"with","start":1.7799999713897705,"end":2.0999999046325684},{"word":"a","start":2.0999999046325684,"end":2.4600000381469727},{"word":"tall","start":2.4600000381469727,"end":2.619999885559082},{"word":"chimney","start":2.619999885559082,"end":2.940000057220459},{"word":"built","start":2.940000057220459,"end":3.640000104904175},{"word":"in","start":3.640000104904175,"end":3.880000114440918},{"word":"1813","start":3.880000114440918,"end":4.820000171661377},{"word":"to","start":4.820000171661377,"end":5.079999923706055},{"word":"1814","start":5.079999923706055,"end":5.980000019073486},{"word":"at","start":5.980000019073486,"end":6.440000057220459},{"word":"Wylam","start":6.440000057220459,"end":6.760000228881836},{"word":"Colliery","start":6.760000228881836,"end":7.340000152587891},{"word":"in","start":7.340000152587891,"end":7.579999923706055},{"word":"the","start":7.579999923706055,"end":7.940000057220459},{"word":"north","start":7.940000057220459,"end":7.940000057220459},{"word":"of","start":7.940000057220459,"end":8.460000038146973},{"word":"England","start":8.460000038146973,"end":8.460000038146973},{"word":"by